# YSL L’Homme V4 — Inventory-Fit Spice-Open Chassis

**Status:** Working research build. It is not an authenticated YSL formula, a passed sensory equivalence result, a safety authorization, or a regulatory certificate.

## Verdict

This is the **best practical chassis for the currently stated inventory limits**. The expanded V3 target remains the more chemically faithful reconstruction hypothesis, but it cannot be built as written because it contains materials that are not available. This V4 preserves the V3 structural intent while making every listed bench addition compatible with the current inventory assumptions.

The architecture remains:

```text
4,500 µL total concentrate
= 4,200 µL fixed spice-neutral core
+   212 µL non-spice interface bridge
+    88 µL replaceable spice socket
```

For bench work, the duplicated core and bridge rows are consolidated into **54 unique additions totaling 4,412 µL**, followed by one 88 µL spice module or one 88 µL DPG neutral control.

## Current inventory assumptions

This build assumes the following currently owned stocks:

- Galaxolide 80% in ethanol
- Romandolide neat
- Zenolide neat
- Ambrettolide 10% in DPG
- Exaltolide 10% in DPG
- Alpha Isomethyl Ionone neat
- Orivone neat
- Ultralia neat
- Alpha Irone available as a 10% working solution
- Dihydro Beta Ionone available and prepared as a 10% working solution
- Benzyl Salicylate neat
- Leafovert, provisionally treated as neat
- Hexyl Acetate neat, from which a 1% working solution is prepared

> **Stop condition:** If Romandolide, Zenolide, Ambrettolide, Leafovert, or the listed stock strengths are not actually available, do not mix this version. Recalculate the affected block rather than making an undocumented substitution.

## Materials removed from the prior build

- Ethylene Brassylate
- Habanolide
- Muscenone Delta
- Ethyl Linalool
- Isoraldeine 95
- Bacdanol
- Cis-3-Hexenyl Salicylate
- Methyl Ionone Gamma Coeur
- Lavandin Grosso Oil
- Caryophyllene Acetate
- Peranat
- Geranyl Acetate
- Neobutenone Alpha
- Neryl Acetate
- Liffarome
- Pear Ester
- Citronellyl Acetate
- Dihydro Alpha Ionone
- Heliotropin (only Heliotropin Fleuressence is available)

The fixed chassis also contains **none of the original spice signature**:

- Fresh Ginger Oil
- Black Pepper Oil
- Cardamom Oil
- Nutmeg Oil
- Coriander Seed Oil
- Basil Oil, ct. Methyl Chavicol
- Elemi Oil
- Cinnamon Bark Oil

That leaves the 88 µL socket genuinely open for a new spice direction.

## Main substitution logic

| Missing or unsuitable target material | V4 treatment | Why this is preferable to the prior build |
|---|---|---|
| Ethylene Brassylate + Habanolide + Muscenone Delta | Galaxolide 80%, Romandolide, Zenolide, Ambrettolide 10%, Exaltolide 10%, and DPG | Uses confirmed available musks and preserves the original musk-block active arithmetic more closely than simply overloading Galaxolide |
| Ethyl Linalool | Linalool + Linalyl Acetate + Dihydromyrcenol | Preserves the fresh floral-citrus bridge, while explicitly admitting that tenacity and polish will differ |
| Isoraldeine 95 | Alpha Isomethyl Ionone | Closest available violet-orris grade-level replacement |
| Methyl Ionone Gamma Coeur | Orivone + Ultralia + Alpha Isomethyl Ionone + Alpha Irone 10% | Better than collapsing the entire missing ionone function into more Alpha Isomethyl Ionone; preserves buttery, diffusive, powdery, and rooty facets separately |
| Bacdanol | Additional Sandalore | Preserves sandalwood rounding, though with less force and diffusion |
| Cis-3-Hexenyl Salicylate | Benzyl Salicylate + Leafovert + Cis-3-Hexenol 1% | Recreates leafy salicylate function using available materials, while remaining clearly labeled as a functional reconstruction |
| Lavandin Grosso | Linalool + Linalyl Acetate + Petitgrain Mandarin | Keeps aromatic lift without placing an unavailable natural into the build |
| Peranat, Neobutenone Alpha, Liffarome, and Pear Ester | Allyl Amyl Glycolate, Allyl Cyclohexyl Propionate, Leafovert, Helional, Cis-3-Hexenol, and Hexyl Acetate 1% | Rebuilds the green-fruity-water bridge from available materials instead of leaving dead rows |
| Geranyl, Neryl, and Citronellyl Acetates | Linalyl Acetate, Benzyl Acetate, Bergamot, and Geraniol 10% | Maintains floral-citrus ester continuity with available stocks |
| Dihydro Alpha Ionone | Dihydro Beta Ionone 10% | Keeps a dry leafy-violet trace with an explicitly non-equivalent identity |
| Heliotropin 10% | Small increases to Coumarin 20%, Vanillin 10%, and DPG | Avoids silently treating opaque Heliotropin Fleuressence as pure Heliotropin |

